{{Evolved_Card_Infobox|Cost=3|CycleCost=2|Rarity=Common|Arena=Barbarian Bowl|Type=Building}}
{{Quote|When this Evolution is deployed, it barrages both sides of the Arena, dealing damage and knocking enemies back. Who doesn't love the smell of gunpowder in the morning?}}

The Cannon's Evolution is a {{Rarity|Common}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked with 6 Evolution Shards. It spawns a Cannon with identical stats to the original. After deployment, the Cannon shoots 9 cannonballs in 2 rows, 5 on the top row and 4 on the bottom, which deals area damage and inflicts knockback. It appears as a large dark metal barrel mounted on a four-legged wooden mount with a purple metal plate, legs and supports reinforced with gold chains, with a purple muzzle, two team-colored ridges, one midway and the other at the rear, along with a [[Card Evolution]] symbol in between, and a metal wing attached to both sides. The Cannon's Evolution costs 3 [[Elixir]] and requires 2 cycles to deploy.

==Strategy==
*The Evolved Cannon can be used offensively to snipe buildings and troops on the opponents side of the [[Arenas|Arena]].
*The knock back can push units towards the Cannon, making it great on defense.
*When a tower is down, placing the Cannon on the opponent's side would actually hit the other towers (however, it does reduced damage to them, but this is still beneficial, especially during Sudden Death).
*Against the [[Goblin Barrel/Evolution|Evolved Goblin Barrel]], the Evolved Cannon can prevent all but one hit on either [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Tower]] when using the [[Tower Princess]]. However, it has to be placed in front of the [[King's Tower|King Tower]] to do this, which will prevent it from distracting any other incoming troop, either from the Evolved Goblin Barrel push or from follow-up attacks.
